.Dd $Mdocdate: September 19 2026 $
.Dt EXECV 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm execv ,
.Nm execl ,
.Nm execle
.Nd execute a file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In unistd.h
.Vt extern char **environ;
.Ft int
.Fn execv "const char *path" "char *const argv[]"
.Ft int
.Fn execl "const char *path" "const char *arg" ...
.Ft int
.Fn execle "const char *path" "const char *arg" ... "char *const envp[]"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions replace the current process image with a new process image
constructed from the file at the specified
.Fa path .
They are front-ends for the
.Xr execve 2
system call; see that manual page for detailed information
about the replacement of the current process.
.Pp
The
.Fn execv
function receives the argument list for the new process in the form of a
.Dv NULL Ns -terminated
array of pointers to NUL-terminated strings.
The first argument, by convention, should point to the file name associated
with the file being executed.
Calling
.Fn execv
is equivalent to calling
.Xr execve 2
and passing the
.Va environ
array as the last parameter.
.Pp
The
.Fn execl
and
.Fn execle
functions receive each element of the same
.Dv NULL Ns -terminated
argument array as a separate function parameter, that is,
.Fa arg
and the subsequent ellipsis can be thought of as
.Fa argv[0] ,
.Fa argv[1] ,
\&...,
.Fa argv[argc] .
For
.Fn execl ,
the environment for the new process image is again taken
from the external variable
.Va environ
in the current process.
.Pp
The
.Fn execle
function specifies the environment of the new process by following the
.Dv NULL
pointer that terminates the list of arguments in the parameter list
with a
.Dv NULL Ns -terminated
array of pointers to NUL-terminated strings, each one conventionally
being of the form
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
If any of these functions return, an error has occurred.
The return value is \-1, and the global variable
.Va errno
is set to indicate the error.
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn execv
may fail and set
.Va errno
for any of the errors specified for the library function
.Xr execve 2 .
.Pp
.Fn execl
and
.Fn execle
may also fail and set
.Va errno
for any of the errors specified for the library function
.Xr mmap 2 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr execve 2 ,
.Xr fork 2 ,
.Xr ktrace 2 ,
.Xr ptrace 2 ,
.Xr execvp 3 ,
.Xr environ 7
.Sh STANDARDS
.Fn execv ,
.Fn execl ,
and
.Fn execle
conform to
.St -p1003.1-88 .
.Sh HISTORY
The functions
.Fn execv
and
.Fn execl
first appeared in
.At v2 .
The functions
.Fn execve
and
.Fn execle
first appeared in
.At v7 .
